[size=4][u]Standing Orders[/u][/size]

Standing Orders adds a lightweight interface that lets you clone a Repeat Orders queue from one of player's ship to any number of other player-owned ships - and edit that queue before it is applied.

[size=3][u][b]Features[/b][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] Clone a ship’s running Repeat Orders onto any selection of eligible targets in a single confirmation step.
[*] Works with [b]any[/b] order that can be placed under Repeat Orders, not just trade orders - every parameter of every order is copied.
[*] Review and edit the queue before applying it, shown exactly as the map's [b]Behaviour[/b] tab shows it.
[*] Optionally apply the edited queue back to the source ship as well.
[*] Automatically scales cargo amounts (if used as params) to each target’s hold size, matching the transport type the order actually uses.
[/list]
[size=3][u][b]Requirements[/b][/u][/size]
[list]
[*] [b]X4: Foundations[/b] 8.00 and 9.00. For 7.60 use the version 1.00 (as 2.00 required mods requires 8.00).
[*] [b]Mod Support APIs[/b] by [url=https://next.nexusmods.com/profile/sirnukes?gameId=2659]SirNukes[/url] to be installed and enabled. Version [b]1.95[/b] and upper is required.
[list]
[*] It is available via Steam - [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2042901274]SirNukes Mod Support APIs[/url]
[*] Or via the Nexus Mods - [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/x4foundations/mods/503]Mod Support APIs[/url]
[/list]
[*] `Options Helper`, to provide the in-game Debug Level option. Version [b]1.10[/b] and upper is required.
[list]
[*] It is available via Steam - [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3715253556]Options Helper[/url]
[*] Or via the Nexus Mods - [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/x4foundations/mods/2089]Options Helper[/url]
[/list]
[*] `Print Extension List`, to record the game version and the enabled extensions in the log. Version [b]1.01[/b] and upper is required.
[list]
[*] It is available via Steam - [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3770927339]Print Extension List[/url]
[*] Or via the Nexus Mods - [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/x4foundations/mods/2191]Print Extension List[/url]
[/list]
[/list]
[size=3][u][b]Installation[/b][/u][/size]

You can download the latest version via Steam client - [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3596138453]Standing Orders[/url]
Or you can do it via the Nexus Mods - [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/x4foundations/mods/1871]Standing Orders[/url]

[size=3][u][b]Usage[/b][/u][/size]

This mods adds a several context menu options to the map UI when you right-click on a player-owned ships.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StandingOrders/refs/heads/main/docs/images/repeat_orders_example.png[/img]

[size=3][u][i]Selecting Source Ship[/i][/u][/size]

To select a source ship (the one whose Repeat Orders you want to clone), right-click on it in the map view and choose [b][∞]: Select as Source[/b] from the context menu.
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StandingOrders/refs/heads/main/docs/images/select_as_source.png[/img]

You will get warning messages if source ship is invalid. Some examples:
[list]
[*] the selected ship does not have any valid cargo.
[/list]
  [img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StandingOrders/refs/heads/main/docs/images/no_valid_cargo.png[/img]
[list]
[*] the selected ship has no active Repeat Orders enabled.
[/list]
  [img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StandingOrders/refs/heads/main/docs/images/no_repeat_orders_enabled.png[/img]

If the source ship is valid, map will be centered on it and ship will be selected on a map.

[size=3][u][i]Selecting Target Ships for Cloning Orders[/i][/u][/size]

To clone the Repeat Orders from the selected source ship to other player-owned ships, simple select them on a map or in the list, then right-click and choose [b][∞]: Clone Standing Orders from <source ship>[/b] from the context menu.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StandingOrders/refs/heads/main/docs/images/clone_context_menu.png[/img]

Again, you will get warning messages if no valid target ships are selected.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StandingOrders/refs/heads/main/docs/images/no_valid_targets.png[/img]

[size=3][u][i]Cloning Dialog[/i][/u][/size]

After selecting valid target ships, you will get a dialog showing the summary of the cloning operation.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StandingOrders/refs/heads/main/docs/images/clone_dialog.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StandingOrders/refs/heads/main/docs/images/clone_dialog_to_multiple.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StandingOrders/refs/heads/main/docs/images/clone_dialog_to_mutiple_edited.png[/img]

You can confirm or cancel the operation.
In addition, you can [b]Deselect as Source[/b] ship if you want to choose a different source ship.

[size=3][u][i]Deselecting Source Ship[/i][/u][/size]

To deselect the current source ship, right-click on it in the map view and choose [b][∞]: Deselect as Source[/b] from the context menu.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StandingOrders/refs/heads/main/docs/images/deselect_source_ship.png[/img]

[size=3][u][i]Result of Cloning[/i][/u][/size]

After confirming the cloning operation, the selected target ships will receive the cloned Repeat Orders from the source ship.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StandingOrders/refs/heads/main/docs/images/source_ship.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StandingOrders/refs/heads/main/docs/images/cloned_ship_without_changes.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StandingOrders/refs/heads/main/docs/images/cloned_ship_with_another_capacity_and_edited_order.png[/img]

[size=3][u][b]Extension Options[/b][/u][/size]

The mod adds a [b]Standing Orders[/b] page to [b]Settings[/b] - `Extensions Options`, with a single setting:
[list]
[*] [b]Debug Level[/b] - how much the mod writes to the game log. [b]None[/b] is the default and keeps the log clean, [b]Debug[/b] records one line per action taken, and [b]Trace[/b] adds the per-ship and per-order detail. Use [b]Debug[/b] or [b]Trace[/b] when preparing a bug report, then set it back to `None`.
[/list]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StandingOrders/refs/heads/main/docs/images/options.png[/img]

The setting takes effect immediately, no reload needed.

